    "Chișinău: historic Moldavian Romanian Cyrillic Кишинъу and edited English Kischenau from 1801; imperial Russian Кишиневъ from treaty 1812-05-28; Romanian Chișinău from union 1918-04-09; Latin Moldavian/Russian transitional co-names 1940-08-02; Soviet Cyrillic Moldavian Кишинэу + Russian Кишинёв from legal effective date 1941-03-01; Romanian again from governorate legislation 1941-09-03; Soviet co-names restored at user-chosen treaty 1944-09-12 (not military recapture 08-24); Latin Chișinău state-language name only from 1989-08-31. All sovereignty/language event thresholds are editorial naming selections, not automatic urban renamings.",
